    {
      "id": "ee01f910fe0c4bf3a982669059056eb1f080b623",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 416202614,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I don't remember seeing Piotr on gitlab yet, I doubt he'd mind a direct email. His name didn't auto-complete when I tried to add him as an assignee (which I'm sure you probably tried too).\n\nI remember being confused by this - I was sure I had seen the problem at the time with current master, but after discussion when I tried there was no issue.  Maybe I saw the dissector_assert in a valgrind call stack, but just loading the capture worked Ok.\n\nI didn't find it very satisfactory to rely upon different behaviour of proto_item_set_len() and proto_item_set_end() when they see an error (i.e. one throws and one doesn't), and maybe not leave a clear indication of what had gone wrong. On the other hand, I doubt there are many implementations of the kafka protocol - you either have the frame properly passed to the dissector, or you don't.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
